yidslots for OS-9/68000=======================ORIG holds comp.sources.games volume 5, yid-slots, as posted: BobGlickstein's slot machine whose three windows spin through parts of Jewishnames, with the name and payoff list beside it.  The files next to ORIGbuild the OS-9 program.The post's terms ask that the copyright notice stay on every file and inthe program's own introduction -- it prints "(c) 1987 by Bob Glickstein"at start-up, and that is untouched -- and that any modification be noted.This file is that notice.What changed, and why:  yid-slots.h  Under OSK the name file is /dd/GAMES/YIDSLOTS/yid-names.               The post's default was /usr/games/yid-names, and a file               named on the command line still overrides it.  recipe       -Drandom=rand -Dsrandom=srand: the default libraries have               no random().  The module is named yidslots, without the               hyphen: no program name on this disk carries one, and the               catalogue's own index parser does not accept one.  The               source files keep their posted names.yid-slots.c builds unchanged.  This curses library has the wscanw(),overwrite() and scrollok() the program needs.Data: GAMES/YIDSLOTS/yid-names, the list as posted -- three groups of nameparts separated by `*', then the paying combinations, `?' matching any part.Build: cc yid-slots.c -DOSK -Drandom=rand -Dsrandom=srand -l=curses.l          -l=termlib.l